<section id="s-the-view-layer">
<span id="the-view-layer"></span><h2>The view layer<a href="#the-view-layer" title="Link to this heading">¶</a></h2>
<p>Django has the concept of “views” to encapsulate the logic responsible for
processing a user’s request and for returning the response. Find all you need
to know about views via the links below:</p>
<ul>
<li><p><strong>The basics:</strong>
<a href="topics/http/urls/"><span>URLconfs</span></a> |
<a href="topics/http/views/"><span>View functions</span></a> |
<a href="topics/http/shortcuts/"><span>Shortcuts</span></a> |
<a href="topics/http/decorators/"><span>Decorators</span></a> |
<a href="topics/async/"><span>Asynchronous Support</span></a></p></li>
<li><p><strong>Reference:</strong>
<a href="ref/views/"><span>Built-in Views</span></a> |
<a href="ref/request-response/"><span>Request/response objects</span></a> |
<a href="ref/template-response/"><span>TemplateResponse objects</span></a></p></li>
<li><p><strong>File uploads:</strong>
<a href="topics/http/file-uploads/"><span>Overview</span></a> |
<a href="ref/files/file/"><span>File objects</span></a> |
<a href="ref/files/storage/"><span>Storage API</span></a> |
<a href="topics/files/"><span>Managing files</span></a> |
<a href="howto/custom-file-storage/"><span>Custom storage</span></a></p></li>
<li><p><strong>Class-based views:</strong>
<a href="topics/class-based-views/"><span>Overview</span></a> |
<a href="topics/class-based-views/generic-display/"><span>Built-in display views</span></a> |
<a href="topics/class-based-views/generic-editing/"><span>Built-in editing views</span></a> |
<a href="topics/class-based-views/mixins/"><span>Using mixins</span></a> |
<a href="ref/class-based-views/"><span>API reference</span></a> |
